GL: upload only the uniforms whose value changed for the program (perf audit finding 13).
bgfx's GL backend re-uploaded every uniform of a program (commit of ProgramGL::m_constantBuffer) whenever any
uniform of a draw changed or the program changed: 75-150 KB of glUniform* per frame for ~70 committing draws, of
which the shim really changed ~17 KB. A GL program object keeps its uniform values, so each ProgramGL now keeps a
shadow of the values it holds and commit() uploads only the uniforms that differ from it; a program switch uploads
nothing the program already has. The shadow lives and dies with the GL program (init / destroy), starts invalid
(GL zeroes a linked or binary-loaded program's uniforms) and is cleared by the one upload outside commit() (the
blitter's sampler). All of it runs on the render thread, so bgfx's multithreaded mode needs nothing more.
Upstream has a per-(GL program id, location) hash-map cache for the same purpose (BGFX_GL_CONFIG_UNIFORM_CACHE,
Emscripten only): a map lookup per vec4 register, never reset when GL reuses a deleted program's id. Not taken.
bgfx::gl::g_stormUniformUploadCalls / Bytes count every glUniform* the backend issues (engine render metrics).

